          "path": "_m/d/n/t/8/abingdon-virginia-wp/a-wedding-interrupted-by-war-7.jpg",
          "filename": "A Wedding Interrupted by War (7393904498).jpg",
          "caption": "\"War affected every aspect of life on the homefront. While occupying Confederate Colonel Samuel Fulkerson’s home in 1864, Union troops raided his sister Kate’s\nwedding. An African-American woman formerly enslaved on the estate later recalled that soldiers stormed the banquet and stole the wedding rings. The bride and groom escaped (unmarried), returning a few days later for the ceremony.\" (Abingdon, Virginia, Overmountain Victory National Historic Trail)",
          "alt": "\"War affected every aspect of life on the homefront. While occupying Confederate Colonel Samuel Fulkerson’s home in 1864, Union troops raided his sister Kate’s\nwedding. An African-American woman formerly enslaved on the estate later recalled that soldiers stormed the banquet and stole the wedding rings. The bride and groom escaped (unmarried), returning a few days later for the ceremony.\" (Abingdon, Virginia, Overmountain Victory National Historic Trail)",
          "width": 597,
          "height": 814,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "TradingCardsNPS",
