          "path": "_m/d/n/t/8/abingdon-virginia-wp/abingdon-muster-grounds-abingd.jpg",
          "filename": "Abingdon Muster Grounds, Abingdon, Virginia. Preserved portion of the original muster field where Virginia patriot militia (17528ee4-1dd8-b71c-07b3-a577545f7061).jpg",
          "caption": "A green field inside a wooden fence with trees and homes visible in the background.\nAbingdon Muster Grounds, Abingdon, Virginia.  Preserved portion of the original muster field where Virginia patriot militia gathered on September 23, 1780, then left the following day to begin the Kings Mountain campaign.  Owned and operated by the Town of Abingdon, Virgina, with a visitor center, trails, and special activities.\nKeywords: abingdon; virginia; overmountain",
          "alt": "A green field inside a wooden fence with trees and homes visible in the background.\nAbingdon Muster Grounds, Abingdon, Virginia.  Preserved portion of the original muster field where Virginia patriot militia gathered on September 23, 1780, then left the following day to begin the Kings Mountain campaign.  Owned and operated by the Town of Abingdon, Virgina, with a visitor center, trails, and special activities.\nKeywords: abingdon; virginia; overmountain",
          "width": 1538,
          "height": 1213,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "NPS photo",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abingdon_Muster_Grounds,_Abingdon,_Virginia._Preserved_portion_of_the_original_muster_field_where_Virginia_patriot_militia_(17528ee4-1dd8-b71c-07b3-a577545f7061).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "abingdon-virginia-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "dnt8",
          "smallPath": "_m/d/n/t/8/abingdon-virginia-wp/abingdon-muster-grounds-abingd-small.webp"
